max_handshakes_count = max_handshakes(n_people)
print(max_handshakes_count)
```

When we run this code, it will output `231`, confirming our mathematical calculation.

### Conclusion

Both the mathematical analysis and the Python program lead us to the same conclusion. Therefore, the maximum possible number of handshakes at the party with 22 attendees is:

\[
\boxed{231}
\]
