\[
\text{Total score before last test} = 91n
\]

Now, if Brian scores 98 on his last test, the total score after including the last test becomes:

\[
\text{Total score after last test} = 91n + 98
\]

The new arithmetic mean after including the last test is given as 92. Since he will have taken \( n + 1 \) tests in total (including the last test), we can express the new mean as:

