The line \( A + B = 165 \) intersects the axes at points that are outside the square defined by \( 0 \leq A \leq 60 \) and \( 0 \leq B \leq 60 \). Specifically, the line intersects the x-axis at \( A = 165 \) (which is outside the square) and the y-axis at \( B = 165 \) (also outside the square). Therefore, the line \( A + B = 165 \) does not intersect the square at all.

Since the condition \( A + B < 165 \) is always satisfied for any \( A \) and \( B \) within the square, we conclude that the entire area of the square is valid.

The area of the square is:

\[
