A number is a multiple of \(11\) if the difference between the sum of the digits in odd positions and the sum of the digits in even positions is a multiple of \(11\). For \(N = abba\), the odd-position digits are \(a\) and \(b\), and the even-position digits are \(b\) and \(a\). The difference is:

